{{!-- **Where the pace comes from, written in the order it is worked out.**

      The load allows a speed; hunger takes feet off it; what is left is what
      this character marches at. That chain used to be an arrow and a number at
      the right end of the weight track, which gave the answer and hid every
      term of it (Dolmenmaster, 2026-08-31: *"vielleicht lässt sich die
      Spielergeschwindigkeit noch etwas besser darstellen statt dem Pfeil und
      der Zahl? irgendwie werden ja auch die Mali verrechnet"*).

      **Outline is what the load allows, filled is what you actually get.** Both
      figures are badges of the same size and the same tier colour, so the
      starting value is as easy to read as the result — the mali stand between
      them and the equals sign says which is which.

      Where nothing is taken off, the two numbers are the same and only the
      filled one is drawn: an equation with no terms is just its answer.

      The number is footSpeed, this character's own pace, and NOT finalSpeed —
      which a slow pack animal drags down. That belongs to the party, and the
      party has the convoy row above to say it in. --}}
<div class="speed-readout">
  <span class="enc-label">{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Encumbrance.Speed"}}</span>

  {{#if (gt encumbrance.hungerSpeedLoss 0)}}
  <span class="speed-base {{speedColor encumbrance.loadSpeed}}"
        title="{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.BaseHint"}}">
    {{speedLabel encumbrance.loadSpeed}}
  </span>
  <span class="speed-op" aria-hidden="true">&minus;</span>
  <span class="speed-malus"
        title="{{#if encumbrance.hungerFloored}}{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.HungerHintFloored" penalty=encumbrance.hungerSpeedPenalty loss=encumbrance.hungerSpeedLoss}}{{else}}{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.HungerHint" penalty=encumbrance.hungerSpeedPenalty}}{{/if}}">
    <i class="fas fa-drumstick-bite"></i> {{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.Hungry" n=encumbrance.hungerSpeedLoss}}
  </span>
  <span class="speed-op" aria-hidden="true">=</span>
  {{/if}}

  <span class="speed-result {{speedColor encumbrance.footSpeed}}"
        title="{{#if (gt encumbrance.hungerSpeedLoss 0)}}{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.ResultHint" base=(speedLabel encumbrance.loadSpeed) loss=encumbrance.hungerSpeedLoss}}{{else}}{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.ResultHintPlain"}}{{/if}}">
    {{speedLabel encumbrance.footSpeed}}
  </span>

  {{!-- Hungry, and it costs nothing: a load that already has them down to 10 ft
        cannot be slowed further, because Speed is never reduced below 10. The
        sum above would then read "10 − 0 = 10", so hunger is kept out of it and
        said here instead — silence would have been the one wrong answer, with
        the day bar calling them starving three windows over. --}}
  {{#if (and (gt encumbrance.hungerSpeedPenalty 0) (eq encumbrance.hungerSpeedLoss 0))}}
  <span class="speed-malus speed-malus-spent"
        title="{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.FloorHint" penalty=encumbrance.hungerSpeedPenalty}}">
    <i class="fas fa-drumstick-bite"></i> {{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.Floor"}}
  </span>
  {{/if}}

  {{!-- How much further the pack may grow before the pace drops a step. The
        tick marks on the track hold the same fact, but only one hover at a
        time, and only in weight mode is there a single track to answer it. --}}
  {{#if (eq encumbrance.mode "weight")}}
  {{#if (gt encumbrance.totalWeight 1600)}}
  <span class="speed-headroom speed-headroom-over"
        title="{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.OverMaxHint"}}">
    <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> {{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.OverMax"}}
  </span>
  {{else if encumbrance.nextTierSpeed}}
  <span class="speed-headroom"
        title="{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.HeadroomHint" wt=encumbrance.weightToNextTier speed=(speedLabel encumbrance.nextTierSpeed)}}">
    {{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.Headroom" wt=encumbrance.weightToNextTier speed=(speedLabel encumbrance.nextTierSpeed)}}
  </span>
  {{else}}
  <span class="speed-headroom"
        title="{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.StandstillHint"}}">
    {{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.Standstill" wt=encumbrance.weightToNextTier}}
  </span>
  {{/if}}
  {{/if}}

  {{!-- Slot mode only: which of the two tracks is setting the pace. --}}
  {{#if (neq encumbrance.bottleneck "none")}}
  <span class="enc-bottleneck" title="{{localize "DOLMENWOOD.Speed.BottleneckHint"}}">
    ⚠ {{bottleneckLabel encumbrance.bottleneck}}
  </span>
  {{/if}}
</div>
